# ⚠ Device scripts must stay LF. A CRLF `#!/system/bin/sh` fails on Android with
# a "not found" that names the interpreter, not the line endings -- an hour lost
# to a one-byte problem.
*.sh text eol=lf

# ⚠⚠ A patch must stay LF too, and for a sharper reason than a shell script:
# `git apply` compares CONTEXT lines byte for byte against an LF source tree, so
# a patch checked out with CRLF fails with "patch does not apply" and says
# nothing about line endings. CI builds on Linux and would have been fine; a
# contributor on Windows committing one would not.
*.patch text eol=lf
*.diff text eol=lf
